  "summary": "One SQL admission transaction retains exactly one approved implementation owner per repository issue, defers other factory/mythical work, and authorizes only original observation/cancellation after mutable registration changes.",
  "eligibility": "Only enabled repository-job GitHub issue/issues/issue_comment dispatches with explicit TODO label configuration participate, alongside approved issue-backed mythical items. Declaration alone, ordinary roles/direct events, trials, schedules and nonfactory jobs do not claim.",
  "acceptance": {
    "race": "Real PG simultaneous mythical/role admission, exact expected owner and typed loser, repeated five times; no unrelated precondition failures accepted.",
    "retention": "Duplicate delivery, independent restarted service, active run after admission completion, disabled/replaced registration, same-text mythical phase gap retain owner/reason.",
    "handoff": "Canonical terminal or proven no-launch cancellation only; revised approved generation waits until all old mythical operations are quiet.",
    "authority": "Original user/workspace/run and separate reply operation snapshot permit only observation/cancellation; new/replaced users, registration, scope and fresh approval rejected.",
    "upgrade": "Actual in-flight canonical admission blocks upgrade before backfill and retains exact operation; legacy ambiguous owners remain fenced, queued followers acquire no owner, migration ledger replay stable.",
